</task>

<task type="tracer">
  <name>Task 1: End-to-end lang.interface/1 slice — one path, producer to projection</name>
  <files>internal/compiler/core/core.go, internal/compiler/originvalidate/originvalidate.go, internal/compiler/protocol/protocol.go, internal/compiler/session/session.go, internal/compiler/originvalidate/originvalidate_test.go</files>
  <read_first>
    - internal/compiler/core/core.go:148-171 — the exact `Interface`, `InterfaceSchema`, `FunctionSignature`, `Parameter` declarations being widened, plus the "structurally cannot reach a body" doc-comment claim that must survive the widening verbatim in spirit
    - internal/compiler/core/core.go:5-8 — the `Schema`/`Schema1` versioned-const pairing this bump copies exactly
    - internal/compiler/core/core.go:60-64 — `ForeignContract`'s plain-string `Unwind`/`NonlocalExit`/`Fails` fields; the in-tree precedent for `ForeignReach`'s three fields and the `Fails` vocabulary reused verbatim
    - internal/compiler/originvalidate/originvalidate.go:405-434 — `digest()` and `BuildInterface`, including the exact-ID lookup at :427 with its silent empty-abilities fallback
    - internal/compiler/session/session.go:1023-1064 — `InterfaceExportCommandFile`, the real producer entry point (CONTEXT.md's `RunInterfaceCommandFile` does not exist — amendment A-04)
    - internal/compiler/protocol/protocol.go:125-150 — `InterfaceSummary` / `InterfaceFunctionAnswer`, the "never from a body field" consumer
    - .planning/phases/07-calls-signatures-and-call-graph-refusal/07-PATTERNS.md — section "internal/compiler/core/core.go — lang.interface/1", Analogs A/B/C/D
  </read_first>
  <action>
Wire ONE path end to end: a single existing single-function fixture producing a
complete `lang.interface/1` document that reaches the protocol projection. No
peer yet, no seeded faults yet, no other call sites.

In `internal/compiler/core/core.go`, keep the existing
`const InterfaceSchema = "lang.interface/0"` line untouched and add the sibling
`const InterfaceSchema1 = "lang.interface/1"`, following the `Schema`/`Schema1`
pairing at `core.go:5-8`. Declare the `/1` types exactly as D-07-09 specifies,
with the JSON tags as written there:
`FunctionSignature{ID, Name, Parameters []ParameterContract, Return ReturnContract, Abilities []Ability, Callable bool, Fails string (omitempty), Foreign ForeignReach, ClosureDigest string}`;
`ParameterContract{ID, Name, Type, Mode, Drops}` with `Mode` one of `owned`,
`shared`, `exclusive` and no legal empty value;
`ReturnContract{Type, Mode, Paths []string, Fresh bool}` with `Paths` empty if
and only if `Mode == "owned"`;
`ForeignReach{Allocator, Unwind, NonlocalExit string}` as plain strings per the
`ForeignContract` precedent at `core.go:60-64` (planner discretion, exercised:
plain strings, not a new enumerated type).

Drop `PublicOrigin` from the `/1` signature — it is subsumed by `ReturnContract`,
which carries the same two access modes but is total rather than optional. Keep
the `PublicOrigin` type itself for `core.Function`.

Every required field carries no `omitempty`, and each field's doc comment states
that absence is an error refused by both producer and peer (D-07-09). Put
D-07-13's integrity-not-authenticity statement on `ClosureDigest`'s doc comment:
it is an unkeyed content hash that detects staleness, never forgery, and the
forgery answer is independent re-derivation.

In `originvalidate.BuildInterface`, emit `Schema: core.InterfaceSchema1` and
populate the `/1` fields for each function from the checked core alone. Reuse the
existing `digest()` helper at `originvalidate.go:405-408` verbatim — the
`"sha256:" + full hex` format — and mint no second digest format.
`ClosureDigest` is D-07-12's Merkle chain over this signature plus its callees'
`ClosureDigest`s — a chain over callee **summary** digests, never over a callee
body. Per **D-07-11**, call-graph **edges are deliberately excluded** from the
summary: an edge list would make every consumer whole-program-aware and re-import
the already-rejected Design A. The summary carries only closure-derived scalars
(`Foreign`, `ClosureDigest`); edges live in `callgraph` (07-04).

`ClosureDigest` for a zero-callee function is the digest of that function's own
`/1` signature bytes with an empty callee-digest list; this is the A-06 base case
and it is decided here explicitly, not left implicit. Every function in today's
corpus is zero-callee, so this base case is the only arm exercised in this plan;
the Merkle-chain arm over callee digests lands with `OpCall` in `07-02-PLAN.md`.

Teach `protocol.InterfaceFunctionAnswer` and `session.InterfaceExportCommandFile`
the `/1` fields so the exported document round-trips through the projection with
no field silently lost. Do not touch any `core.Program` field — the whole point
of `InterfaceSchema`'s independent versioning is that this bump moves no
`core.Program` byte.
  </action>
  <verify>
    <automated>go test ./internal/compiler/originvalidate/... ./internal/compiler/core/... ./internal/compiler/protocol/... ./internal/compiler/session/...</automated>
    <fails_when>non-zero exit, or "no tests to run" in the output</fails_when>
    <automated>go test ./internal/compiler/core/... -run TestPreviousPhaseCoreBytesUnchanged -v</automated>
    <fails_when>non-zero exit, or the output contains "core bytes moved for", or the output does not contain a PASS line for TestPreviousPhaseCoreBytesUnchanged</fails_when>
  </verify>
  <acceptance_criteria>
    - `internal/compiler/core/core.go` declares both `InterfaceSchema` (value `lang.interface/0`) and `InterfaceSchema1` (value `lang.interface/1`) as exported consts.
    - `core.FunctionSignature` has fields `Parameters []ParameterContract`, `Return ReturnContract`, `Callable bool`, `Foreign ForeignReach`, `ClosureDigest string`, and has no `PublicOrigin` field.
    - `ParameterContract.Mode` and `ReturnContract.Mode` carry no `omitempty` JSON tag.
    - `ClosureDigest`'s doc comment contains the words `integrity` and `never` in a sentence stating it does not prove authenticity.
    - `originvalidate.BuildInterface` returns `Schema` equal to `core.InterfaceSchema1`.
    - For every function in `testdata/phase1` through `testdata/phase4`, `BuildInterface` produces a `ClosureDigest` that starts with `sha256:` and is followed by exactly 64 lowercase hex characters, and running `BuildInterface` twice on the same program yields byte-identical digests.
    - `go test ./internal/compiler/core/... -run TestPreviousPhaseCoreBytesUnchanged` passes.
  </acceptance_criteria>
  <done>One existing single-function fixture produces a complete, digest-bound `lang.interface/1` document that reaches `protocol.InterfaceSummary` with no field lost, and no `core.Program` byte moved. Committed.</done>
  <reversibility rating="one-way">Mints `lang.interface/1` (D-07-08) and commits `Parameters` as a slice (D-07-10) — published versioned schema; superseded only additively by a `/2`.</reversibility>
</task>

