Add to `corevalidate` a structural re-derivation of the `lang.interface/1`
signature summary — per-parameter ownership requirement, the return-origin
contract, and abilities — computed from the **checked core artifact alone**, and
refuse on mismatch with the producer's summary. Non-liveness only: interprocedural
loan liveness is Phase 09 and is declared in `PHASE-07-DEBT.md`.

The peer must be a genuinely separate implementation. It must not import
`originvalidate`, must not call `BuildInterface`, and must not be extracted into a
shared helper that both sides call — a single implementation two callers agree
with cannot diverge, which is anti-independence by definition (D-07-22). Its doc
comment follows the `corevalidate.go:352-361` template: name what
`originvalidate.BuildInterface` does, name the materially different mechanism this
one uses (it reads the validator's own replayed place/type state rather than the
producer's type-fact ID lookup), and name the input space it reads instead.

**D-07-21:** wire the peer into **both** `replayStraightLine`
(`corevalidate.go:903`) and `replayBlocks` (`:1098`), with a test that fails if
only one has it. Wiring one
and not the other reproduces the literal D-02-03 / D-03-01 failure — a fix landing
in the wrong half. Instrument each site so the test in Test 2 can assert both
actually ran, rather than inferring it.

Extend `corevalidate`'s existing import-independence falsifier's forbidden-suffix
list with the `originvalidate` package path, following
`pathoracle_test.go:46-76`'s `parser.ImportsOnly` shape.
