<language_surface_constraint>
The language has **no arithmetic, no iteration, no collections, no strings, and
no numeric type beyond `Byte`**. `match` is the only control flow. Every fixture
in this plan is built from: `module`, `export { fn ... }`, `data X = | A | B`,
`fn f(p: T) -> T { ... }`, `let x = borrow y` / `take y` / `try foreign(y)`, a
new `let r = g(x)`, and `match p { Arm => { ... } }`. Do not author a fixture
that needs anything else.
</language_surface_constraint>

