<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| callee module boundary -> caller | the publishable/export surface a caller is permitted to reach across |
| callee summary -> call admission | the `Callable` bit is the deciding fact; the callee body is never opened |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-07-12 | Elevation of privilege | call admission against `FunctionSignature.Callable` | high | mitigate | ASVS V4 analog. Fail-closed refusal with the ratified stable `core.*` code, never a silent drop or a warning. `Callable`'s Go zero value `false` makes absence the refusing case (D-07-09) |
| T-07-13 | Repudiation | the `Callable` derivation | high | mitigate | Derived twice by materially different mechanisms (producer reads type facts; peer reads the program's own export set and function table), with three seeded faults in Task 3 proving each derivation can be observed to fail |
| T-07-14 | Tampering | a forged summary asserting `Callable: true` | medium | mitigate | The peer re-derives from the checked core rather than trusting the summary; the digest detects staleness only (D-07-13), so re-derivation is the forgery answer |
| T-07-15 | Information disclosure | call admission reading a callee body | medium | mitigate | SEM-05's structural claim. Task 1's acceptance criterion asserts the admission arm touches only `core.FunctionSignature`, never `core.Function.Linear`/`Match` |
| T-07-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo/go installs | high | mitigate | No package-manager install task in this plan; the Package Legitimacy Audit records zero new production dependencies |
</threat_model>

