  <action>
Wire ONE path: a direct two-function cycle, refused by `check` before it returns.
No rotation, no 32-cap, no mutation seam yet — those are Task 2 and Task 3.

**Package.** Create `internal/compiler/callgraph` with a package doc following
`pathoracle.go:1-29`'s structure, **with one deviation stated explicitly**:
`pathoracle` is consumed only by tests and the verify harness, but `callgraph` is
imported by `check` **in production**. The doc must say it is consumed by `check`
before it returns a `core.Program`, and never by `corevalidate`, `interp`, or
`cgen` — `corevalidate` runs its own traversal (07-05). Do not copy pathoracle's
"consumed only by tests" claim.

Entry point: `func Order(program core.Program) (reversePostorder []string, err error)`.
Iterative three-color (white / gray / black) DFS over an **explicit stack**, roots
= **all declared functions**, not just the entry point. Native Go recursion is
prohibited — the compile-time traversal must cost no Go stack.

The distinguisher is **on-stack (gray) re-entry**. A node already black is a
legitimately revisited shared node in an acyclic subgraph, not a cycle. Swapping
the gray check for a plain visited set is the highest-value seeded mutation this
phase must kill (07-05), so keep the two states genuinely distinct in the code.

Build edges by enumerating operations with `Kind == core.OpCall` **across all
blocks**, never by block position (D-07-28). **Dedupe edges at graph-build time**
so `E` is bounded by `V²` rather than by operation count; traversal stays `O(V+E)`.
Node identity reuses `isDeclaredFunctionName`'s precedence rule so a declared Lang
function shadowing a foreign symbol cannot silently drop an edge. An edge whose
callee resolves to nothing must **refuse**, never be dropped — a dropped edge is
how a cycle escapes.

Typed error: a private `cycleError` carrying the witness path (`members []string`)
so the diagnostic's ordered `Causes` can be built without re-deriving, with
`Error() string`, `Code() string` returning `"core.call_graph_cycle"`, and an
exported `CycleError(err error) (*cycleError, bool)` accessor.

Add `callgraph`'s own static import-independence test forbidding
`/compiler/corevalidate`, `/compiler/ast`, `/compiler/interp`, `/compiler/cgen`,
and `/compiler/check`.

**Check.** After `check` has emitted `OpCall` for the whole `core.Program`, run
`callgraph.Order` over its **own completed in-memory** program and refuse before
returning it (D-07-14). There is no AST-side graph. A cyclic `core.Program`
therefore exists only as an ephemeral local inside `check` — never returned,
serialized, cached, interpreted, or lowered. Emit the diagnostic with the code and
message ratified at the checkpoint.

**Fixture.** `testdata/phase07/cycle_direct.lang`, module `phase07.cycle_direct`,
two functions that call each other, with a leading `//` comment naming SEM-07 and
D-07-18.
