  <action>
Canonically rotate the cycle's member list so the **lexicographically smallest
function ID sits at index 0** before constructing `Causes`. Without rotation the
same cycle yields a different `Diagnostic.ID` per discovery start order — an
unstable versioned API, because `Causes` participates in ID identity verbatim and
in order.

Declare `truncated:core.call_cycle_bound` as an exported named const in
`protocol` alongside `TruncatedEvidenceTraceBound`, in the same style — declared
once, never a string literal at the emission site. Declare the 32 bound as a named
exported const in `callgraph` with a doc comment following `pathoracle.MaxPaths`'s
pattern: the reachable maximum today, why the constant sits where it does, that it
is fail-closed, and that it is never raised to make a test pass.

Construct the diagnostic with `diagnostic.Error` — **no repairs**, per the
checkpoint. `Primary` is the span of the `OpCall` operation whose edge closes the
canonical cycle.

**Bound the diagnostic, never the traversal.** The 32-cap applies only to emitted
`cycle_member` causes. `Order` still visits every node and edge; a deep acyclic
graph is legal and unbounded (D-07-17). `cycle_length`'s detail carries the true
member count even when the cause list is truncated, so a consumer can tell a
32-cycle from a 400-cycle.
  </action>
