<flagged_assumptions>
**FLAGGED — SEM-07 was returned `unclassified` by the spec-less edge probe and is
NOT silently dropped.**

SEM-07's text includes *"cycles through `Result` matching"*, but `Result` payloads
do not land until **Phase 12**. D-07-28 resolves this **structurally** rather than
by deferral: the `callgraph` builder enumerates operations by
`Kind == core.OpCall` **across all blocks, never by block position**, so calls
inside future `Result` match arms are picked up automatically.

**The assumption this plan must confirm rather than assume:** that the proving
fixture is actually authored and asserted. It is —
`testdata/phase07/call_from_both_match_arms.lang` landed in `07-02-PLAN.md` Task 2,
and Task 2 of this plan adds a **cycle** through both `match` arms so the
enumeration property is exercised against the refusal path, not only the
admission path. If that fixture is missing or its assertion is weakened, the
`Result` half of SEM-07 ships untested — record that explicitly in the SUMMARY
rather than letting it pass.
</flagged_assumptions>

<language_surface_constraint>
No arithmetic, no iteration, no collections, no strings, no numeric type beyond
`Byte`; `match` is the only control flow. Every `.lang` fixture below is built
only from `module`, `export { fn ... }`, `data X = | A | B`, `fn f(p: T) -> T`,
`let x = borrow|take|<call>`, and `match`. The "deep" corpus gets its depth from
**many small functions**, not from long bodies.
</language_surface_constraint>

