<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| synthetic / forged core.Program -> corevalidate | artifacts `check` never produced, which the peer must still refuse |
| check's derivation <-> corevalidate's derivation | two derivations of one fact; their agreement is only evidence if they can disagree |
| corpus -> gate | a gate is only as real as the reachable input space of its corpus |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-07-22 | Repudiation | the two cycle derivations | high | mitigate | D-07-19: `corevalidate` runs its own traversal over a disjoint reachable input space (hand-built synthetic artifacts, no parser, no `check`), never an import of `callgraph`. Enforced by the static import-independence falsifier extended in Task 1 |
| T-07-23 | Tampering | a control that is green but inert | high | mitigate | The gray/black distinction is the entire control, and a chain-only corpus cannot kill its mutation. Task 2's diamond/shared-leaf corpus and Task 3's Test 1 together make the mutation observable. This is M001's recorded failure shape — a green test whose reachable input space omits the hard case |
| T-07-24 | Elevation of privilege | a `callee == caller` edge skip | high | mitigate | Silently legalizes direct recursion. `cycle_self.lang` plus its own seeded mutation (Task 3 Test 2) makes the skip observable |
| T-07-25 | Tampering | an unreachable cycle escaping refusal | high | mitigate | Roots are all declared functions, never just the entry point; `cycle_unreachable.lang` and a synthetic artifact with no entry point at all both refuse |
| T-07-26 | Spoofing | a declared Lang function shadowing a foreign symbol | high | mitigate | Node identity uses `isDeclaredFunctionName`'s precedence rule (`corevalidate.go:1654-1664`); `foreign_symbol_shadowing.lang` is shaped so the cycle is only visible under that rule, so a divergent rule goes red |
| T-07-27 | Tampering | a dropped edge for an unresolvable callee | high | mitigate | Refused through the existing `core.unknown_*` / `core.call_target_not_foreign` path in both derivations, with a seeded drop mutation (Task 3 Test 4) proving the drop is observable |
| T-07-28 | Denial of service | traversal on the deep corpus | medium | accept | Traversal is O(V+E) over an explicit stack with edges deduped at build time (07-04). The deep corpus is bounded by what the parser can express; a 60-second termination bound is asserted rather than a traversal ceiling introduced |
| T-07-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo/go installs | high | mitigate | No package-manager install task in this plan; the Package Legitimacy Audit records zero new production dependencies. `pgregory.net/rapid` is a standing test-only `Adopt` and is not added |
</threat_model>

