     1	// Package pathoracle is Phase 3's third, genuinely different decision
     2	// procedure for loan liveness (03-RESEARCH Q4, ROADMAP criterion 1). It is
     3	// consumed only by tests and the verify harness (session.go) -- never by
     4	// check, corevalidate, interp, or cgen -- and it reads nothing but a
     5	// core.Function's own declared Blocks/Edges/Operations. It imports neither
     6	// check nor corevalidate nor ast, and it calls no production liveness
     7	// function.
     8	//
     9	// Three loan-endpoint derivations now coexist in this repository, and none
    10	// can be obtained from either of the others by renaming (mirroring
    11	// check_test.go's own two-procedure doc-comment convention, extended to
    12	// three):
    13	//
    14	//   - check.go's loanLivenessFixpoint converges a finite lattice of
    15	//     per-block live-loan sets to a fixpoint via a backward worklist: it
    16	//     never enumerates a concrete path, only abstract per-block summaries.
    17	//   - corevalidate.go's recomputeLoanEndpoints materializes an explicit
    18	//     (loan, block, ordinal) use relation and computes ONE bounded
    19	//     reachability closure over it, then reduces to each loan's final
    20	//     reachable uses -- a single global relation, never per-block
    21	//     summaries and never a path.
    22	//   - This package enumerates every DISTINCT acyclic entry-to-return path
    23	//     as an explicit, concrete block sequence, replays each one forward in
    24	//     isolation (never converging or closing anything), and only combines
    25	//     the independent per-path answers at the very end, when a genuine
    26	//     divergence across paths at a fan-out block is what earns a loan its
    27	//     edge endpoint instead of a point endpoint. No shared helper, no
    28	//     queue, and no relation-closure step exists anywhere in this file.
    29	package pathoracle
    30	
    31	import (
    32		"fmt"
    33		"sort"
    34	
    35		"github.com/codename-lang/lang/internal/compiler/core"
    36	)
    37	
    38	// MaxPaths bounds the number of acyclic entry-to-return paths this package
    39	// will enumerate for one function. Today's language caps a match at
    40	// maxArmsPerMatch (64) arms and gives each arm exactly one linear
    41	// entry-to-return path with no nested branching construct, so the real
    42	// reachable maximum is 64 -- MaxPaths is set well above that (a decimal
    43	// order of magnitude) so it never fires on any program the parser can
    44	// produce today, while still being a genuine, finite, fail-closed ceiling
    45	// against a future nested-branching CFG shape (T-03-01/T-03-13): path count
    46	// is multiplicative in branch count for a CFG with more than one level of
    47	// fan-out, so an unbounded enumeration would be a real denial-of-service
    48	// surface the moment that shape becomes reachable.
    49	const MaxPaths = 4096
    50	
    51	// TerminatorKindsOverride is a fault-injection seam for
    52	// TestTerminatorWalkMutationKilled (D-09/D-04-29): production always closes
    53	// a path on the full core.TerminatorKinds() set; the test temporarily
    54	// narrows it (the same "delete OpFail from the recognised set" mutation the
    55	// throwaway-detached-worktree demonstration performs on the source
    56	// directly) to prove that a walker recognising fewer terminators really
    57	// does misclassify a fixture path. nil (the always-true production default)
    58	// means "use core.TerminatorKinds() unmodified".
    59	var TerminatorKindsOverride func() []core.OperationKind
    60	
    61	func recognizedTerminatorKinds() []core.OperationKind {
    62		if TerminatorKindsOverride != nil {
    63			return TerminatorKindsOverride()
    64		}
    65		return core.TerminatorKinds()
    66	}
    67	
    68	// isTerminatorKind is pathoracle's own membership test against the
    69	// terminator registry (D-04-29): a set-membership test against
    70	// core.TerminatorKinds() rather than a literal restatement of it, so
    71	// widening the registry widens this walker automatically.
    72	func isTerminatorKind(kind core.OperationKind) bool {
    73		for _, terminator := range recognizedTerminatorKinds() {
    74			if kind == terminator {
    75				return true
    76			}
    77		}
    78		return false
    79	}
    80	
    81	// RecognizesTerminator is session.go's control:terminator.walk_incomplete
    82	// hook (D-04-29): it reports whether this package's own walker treats kind
    83	// as a terminator, reading the exact same isTerminatorKind this file's
    84	// production walk uses -- never a second, restated copy of the set.
    85	func RecognizesTerminator(kind core.OperationKind) bool { return isTerminatorKind(kind) }
    86	
    87	// pathCapError is returned when a function's acyclic entry-to-return path
    88	// count exceeds MaxPaths. It carries a stable Code(), matching the
    89	// diagnostic.Diagnostic convention used elsewhere in the repository, and
    90	// rejects fail-closed -- the cap is never raised to make a test pass; a
    91	// function that would exceed it is refused, not enumerated.
    92	type pathCapError struct {
